==German==
===Etymology===
From {{etyl|goh|de}} {{term|haso|lang=goh}}, from {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{term/t|gem-pro|*hasô}}, from an Indo-European root originally meaning [[grey]].

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈhaːzə]|lang=de}}
* {{rhymes|aːzə|lang=de}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Hasen|Hasen}}

# {{qualifier|male or female}} [[hare]]
# sometimes mistakenly used for [[rabbit]]

====Declension====
{{de-decl-noun-m|n|n}}

